    "json",
    "Complete this repository task: The `Argument` class in `lib/argument.js` has been reduced to a stub: it no longer interprets its\nname syntax, its setters are not chainable, and choices are neither validated nor collected.\nReimplement it, keeping every current export and method name:\n- `<name>` is a required argument, `[name]` is optional, a bare name is required, and a trailing\n  `...` inside the brackets makes it variadic; `name()` returns the bare name without any of that\n  punctuation;\n- `default()`, `argParser()`, `choices()`, `argRequired()` and `argOptional()` all return the\n  argument so they can be chained;\n- `choices(values)` copies the caller's array, and installs parsing that raises\n  `InvalidArgumentError` with the message `Allowed choices are a, b.` for a value outside the\n  list, and that accumulates values when the argument is variadic;\n- `_collectValue(value, previous)` starts a new array when there is nothing to extend and appends\n  otherwise;\n- `humanReadableArgName` renders the argument back to `<name>`, `[name]`, `<name...>` or\n  `[name...]`.\n\nA command declaring `<first>` and `[rest...]` must pass the first value and an array of the rest\nto its action handler.\nWork only in the current repository. Do not push, open a PR, deploy, or access secrets.\nMake the smallest correct change and run relevant local checks."
  ],
